================================================================================
Scope
================================================================================

The terms above cover the file system itself and everything built from it:

    kext/           the ext2fs kernel extension
    fs/             the ext2fs.fs bundle and its four helper programs
    include/        the shared on-disk and compatibility headers
    installer/      the installer package and disk image
    tests/          the test programs
    Makefile, Makefile.inc, .github/
    tools/com.beako.ext2fs.plist and tools/ext2fs-load
                    the boot-time loader and the LaunchDaemon that runs it

Those sources descend from the Berkeley fast file system by way of the
FreeBSD, NetBSD and OpenBSD ext2fs ports.  Most carry the three-clause form
reproduced above; a few carry the two-clause form, which the three-clause
terms satisfy.  No file in the tree carries the old advertising clause.

tools/ is otherwise a holding area for third-party work, and the terms above
do NOT cover any of the following.  Nothing here relicenses them, and the BSD
terms above must not be read as applying to them:

    tools/e2undel       GNU GPL.  Includes file(1) code by Ian F. Darwin.
    tools/extfsmgr      Apple Public Source License, from ext2fsx.
    vendor/libutil      Apple Public Source License.  Supplies one header,
                        mntopts.h, to mount_ext2fs; no code from it is
                        compiled or linked.
    lib/libkext         BSD 2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2018 lynnl.  Unlike the
                        rest of this list it IS built and linked into the
                        kernel extension.  See lib/libkext/LICENSE.

With the exception of lib/libkext, none of those is built, linked against or
shipped by any target in this repository's Makefiles: the tools/ entries are
kept for reference and SUBDIRS in tools/Makefile is empty.  No part of the
kernel extension, the bundle or the installer is derived from them.

In particular, newfs_ext2fs is not derived from e2fsprogs despite its
mke2fs.c filename; see the note at the top of fs/newfs_ext2fs/mke2fs.c.
